<%# The sign-up screen. POSTs to Devise's registration path with `user[full_name]`,
    `user[username]`, `user[email]`, `user[password]`, `user[password_confirmation]` —
    all frozen, all sanitised by `Users::RegistrationsController`.

    SECURITY: `invisible_captcha :subtitle` (Slice 1) is a spam control, not markup.
    It emits its own wrapper and its own hidden field, and the controller rejects a
    create whose honeypot came back filled. Do not restyle it, do not move it inside a
    field group, and do not touch how it hides itself — the hiding IS the control.

    DESIGN SYSTEM (Slice 9, Task 4.6) — same treatment as the log-in screen: the panel
    is `ui/_card` (white, SQUARE, shadowed), the fields take the field-border token
    plus the indigo focus border instead of a bare uncoloured border resolving to body
    ink, labels are the 14px muted label, and the submit is the `rect` solid button the
    design system assigns to auth screens.

    The password-length hint moves from a Tailwind-default grey onto the design
    system's own muted token; the palette has no grey between those two.

    The design system's `TextField` shows an "@" prefix and real placeholders on the
    username field, but only inside the profile editor — this screen has never rendered
    either, and adding them would be new user-visible copy rather than codification.
%>
<%= render layout: "ui/card", locals: {class: "max-w-md mx-auto mt-16 p-6"} do %>
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-6">Sign up</h2>

  <%= form_for(resource, as: resource_name, url: registration_path(resource_name)) do |f| %>
    <%= render "devise/shared/error_messages", resource: resource %>

    <%= invisible_captcha :subtitle %>

    <div class="mb-3">
      <%= f.label :full_name, class: "block text-sm text-grey mb-1" %>
      <%= f.text_field :full_name, autofocus: true,
            class: "w-full rounded border border-gray-200 px-3 py-2 focus:outline-none focus:border-primary" %>
    </div>
    <div class="mb-3">
      <%= f.label :username, class: "block text-sm text-grey mb-1" %>
      <%= f.text_field :username,
            class: "w-full rounded border border-gray-200 px-3 py-2 focus:outline-none focus:border-primary" %>
    </div>

    <div class="mb-3">
      <%= f.label :email, class: "block text-sm text-grey mb-1" %>
      <%= f.email_field :email, autocomplete: "email",
            class: "w-full rounded border border-gray-200 px-3 py-2 focus:outline-none focus:border-primary" %>
    </div>

    <div class="mb-3">
      <%= f.label :password, class: "block text-sm text-grey mb-1" %>
      <% if @minimum_password_length %>
        <em class="text-xs text-grey">(<%= @minimum_password_length %> characters minimum)</em>
      <% end %>
      <%= f.password_field :password, autocomplete: "new-password",
            class: "w-full rounded border border-gray-200 px-3 py-2 focus:outline-none focus:border-primary" %>
    </div>

    <div class="mb-3">
      <%= f.label :password_confirmation, class: "block text-sm text-grey mb-1" %>
      <%= f.password_field :password_confirmation, autocomplete: "new-password",
            class: "w-full rounded border border-gray-200 px-3 py-2 focus:outline-none focus:border-primary" %>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-4">
      <%= f.submit "Sign up", class: ds_button_classes(variant: :rect) %>
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <%= render "devise/shared/links" %>
<% end %>
